.IX Title "Proc::Killfam 3pm"
.TH Proc::Killfam 3pm 2019-12-10 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Proc::Killfam \- kill a list of pids, and all their sub\-children
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\& use Proc::Killfam;
\& killfam $signal, @pids;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBkillfam\fR accepts the same arguments as the Perl builtin \fBkill\fR command,
but, additionally, recursively searches the process table for children and
kills them as well.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IX Header "EXAMPLE"
\&\fBkillfam 'TERM', ($pid1, \fR\f(CB$pid2\fR\fB, \fR\f(CB@more_pids\fR\fB)\fR;
.SH KEYWORDS
.IX Header "KEYWORDS"
kill, signal
